Description: Fix rekordbox playlist track order on import.

 When Mixxx imports a rekordbox USB it stores each playlist entry keyed by
 the rekordbox `entry_index` in a QMap (sorted by that key), then reads the
 tracks back out by looking up the synthetic indices 1..size via
 QMap::operator[]. That is only correct when `entry_index` is exactly the
 contiguous set {1..N}. Real rekordbox exports routinely write sparse and/or
 non-1-based entry_index values, so the synthetic lookup:
   - pulled tracks into the wrong positions (commonly the trailing tracks of
     the device surfaced at the top of the playlist), and
   - silently inserted phantom track_id=0 rows for every index that had no
     matching key (QMap::operator[] default-inserts on a missing key).

 This became visible once rekordbox-import-fixes.patch corrected the PDB
 row-count parsing so playlists actually populate; before that the playlists
 came in empty and the ordering weakness was hidden.

 Fix: iterate the inner QMap in its natural (entry_index-ascending) key order
 and hand out a fresh 1-based position, instead of looking entries up by a
 synthetic index. Correct for 0-based, 1-based, sparse or permuted
 entry_index, and it never materialises phantom rows.

diff --git a/src/library/rekordbox/rekordboxfeature.cpp b/src/library/rekordbox/rekordboxfeature.cpp
